@{
    ViewData["Title"] = Lang.T("Chimney & Flashing Leak Repair | Charlotte NC", "Reparación de goteras en chimenea y flashing | Charlotte NC");
}
<section class="problem-hero"><div class="site-shell problem-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Chimney and flashing leak repair · Charlotte, NC</p><h1>A chimney leak needs more than another bead of caulk.</h1><p>Water can enter through step flashing, counterflashing, the upslope cricket, roof-to-wall details, masonry or nearby shingles. Majestic documents the roof-side assembly and identifies when masonry work needs a separate specialist.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-gold" href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc#claim-form">@Lang.T("Request free inspection →")</a><a class="button button-ghost" href="tel:+19808005991">@Lang.T("Call Majestic")</a></div></div><figure class="problem-hero-visual"><img src="/damage-guides/chimney-flashing-example.webp" alt="Educational example of damaged chimney flashing and adjacent shingles"/><div class="problem-icon problem-icon-chimney" aria-label="CHIMNEY"><span></span><i></i><b></b></div><figcaption>@Lang.T("Educational damage example · inspection determines the actual condition")</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="problem-urgent"><div class="site-shell"><strong>@Lang.T("SAFETY FIRST")</strong><p>Keep water away from electrical fixtures and finished surfaces. Do not climb onto the roof or chimney. Active fire, smoke, gas or carbon-monoxide concerns belong with emergency authorities and qualified chimney professionals first.</p></div></section><section class="problem-signs section"><div class="site-shell problem-clues-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("What you may notice")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Visible clues help define the inspection—not the final diagnosis.")</h2><p>@Lang.T("Use these examples to describe what you see from a safe location. A photo cannot confirm every roof layer, hidden moisture, cause or repairability.")</p></div><figure class="problem-clue-photo"><img src="/damage-guides/chimney-flashing-example.webp" alt="Educational example of damaged chimney flashing and adjacent shingles"/><figcaption>@Lang.T("Educational reference—not a Majestic customer case.")</figcaption></figure><ul><li>Stain beside the chimney after rain</li><li>Loose, rusted or lifted metal flashing</li><li>Cracked sealant at counterflashing</li><li>Debris or standing water behind the chimney</li><li>Damaged shingles or underlayment at sidewalls</li></ul></div></section><section class="problem-first section" id="first-steps"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("Before the crew arrives")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Five first steps for the homeowner.")</h2></div><p>@Lang.T("Do only what can be completed safely from the ground or a stable interior area.")</p></div><ol><li><span>01</span><p>Record which side of the chimney shows moisture.</p></li><li><span>02</span><p>Note wind direction and rain intensity when it appears.</p></li><li><span>03</span><p>Protect the interior without entering unsafe areas.</p></li><li><span>04</span><p>Avoid applying random roof cement that can hide the actual path.</p></li><li><span>05</span><p>Schedule roof-side and accessible attic inspection.</p></li></ol></div></section><section class="problem-process section"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading centered-heading"><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("How Majestic handles this specific problem")</p><h2>@Lang.T("A documented path from concern to completed roof.")</h2><p>@Lang.T("The exact scope depends on safe access and what the inspection confirms. These five stages show how this particular roof condition is evaluated and repaired.")</p></div><div class="problem-process-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Interior and attic correlation</h3><p>We compare the stain with rafters, sheathing and the roof-to-chimney location.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Flashing assessment</h3><p>We review step flashing, counterflashing, apron, upslope drainage and adjoining shingles.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Scope separation</h3><p>Roof flashing work is distinguished from crown, cap, mortar, brick or fireplace-system repairs.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Layered reconstruction</h3><p>Authorized roof components are opened far enough to rebuild the drainage sequence rather than cover it.</p></article><article><span>05</span><h3>Final documentation</h3><p>Photos show the completed flashing and adjacent roofing details.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="arrival-section section" id="arrival"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("What happens when we arrive")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Six checkpoints from arrival through closeout.")</h2></div><p>@Lang.T("Majestic documents the roof as a construction system, explains choices before work begins and keeps insurance coverage decisions separate from contractor work.")</p></div><div class="arrival-grid"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Arrival, interview and safety check</h3><p>The technician confirms what happened, when the condition was first noticed, whether water is entering now and which interior rooms are affected. Before using a ladder, Majestic checks weather, electrical, tree, structural and fall hazards and explains any access limitation.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Interior and ground-level reference</h3><p>When relevant and accessible, the team starts at the stain, drip or impacted room, reviews the attic from a safe access point and then walks the exterior perimeter. This creates a reference line between the interior evidence and the roof area above it.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Roof-system inspection</h3><p>When safe access is available, Majestic reviews affected slopes plus shingles, ridge and hip caps, valleys, flashing, pipe boots, vents, skylights, roof edges, gutters, fascia and soffit. Wide photographs show location; detail photographs show the condition.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Measurements and factual documentation</h3><p>The record identifies visible conditions, roof geometry, affected components and estimated quantities. Storm-related observations are separated from age, maintenance, installation details and hidden conditions that cannot be confirmed without authorized removal.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h3>Options explained before authorization</h3><p>Majestic explains immediate protection, localized repair, section rebuild and replacement paths when applicable. The homeowner receives a written roofing path and can choose an out-of-pocket project or use the factual documents in a claim they manage with their carrier.</p></div></article><article><span>06</span><div><h3>Construction, verification and closeout</h3><p>After a written scope is approved, materials and schedule are confirmed. Majestic performs the authorized roofing work, controls debris and cleanup, photographs completion and provides the applicable invoice, warranty and project-closeout documents.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="problem-repairs section" id="repairs"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("Repair options")</p><h2>@Lang.T("The inspection determines which option can be built reliably.")</h2></div><p>@Lang.T("Final materials, quantities, code requirements and hidden conditions are confirmed in the written scope.")</p></div><div class="problem-repair-grid"><article><h3>Targeted flashing repair</h3><p>Replace an isolated failed piece when surrounding shingles, underlayment and metal remain compatible.</p></article><article><h3>Flashing rebuild</h3><p>Remove adjacent roofing and reconstruct apron, step and counterflashing details as the assembly requires.</p></article><article><h3>Cricket or back-pan work</h3><p>Improve upslope water diversion where chimney width and roof geometry require it, subject to code and design review.</p></article><article><h3>Masonry coordination</h3><p>A cracked crown, open mortar joint, brick condition or cap problem is referred or coordinated with the appropriate chimney/masonry trade.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="problem-source"><div class="site-shell"><span>i</span><p>Manufacturer installation guidance treats chimney and sidewall flashing as layered metal details, not a surface-only patch. <a href="https://www.owenscorning.com/en-us/roofing/install-instructions/oakridge" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the source ↗</a></p></div></section><section class="faq-section section"><div class="site-shell faq-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("FAQ")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Clear expectations before work begins.")</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>@Lang.T("Is the inspection free?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("Yes. Majestic provides a free roof inspection, photographs, a report, estimated measurements and a written project path, subject to safe access.")</p></details><details><summary>@Lang.T("Does the inspection guarantee insurance coverage?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("No. Majestic documents roofing conditions and scope. The carrier independently decides coverage and payment.")</p></details><details><summary>@Lang.T("Can I pay out of pocket?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("Yes. Majestic can explain an out-of-pocket repair or replacement path as well as the construction documentation used for a claim-related project.")</p></details><details><summary>@Lang.T("How far do you travel?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("Roof inspections are available approximately 90 minutes from Charlotte or Rock Hill, subject to address and schedule confirmation. Raleigh is not in the service area.")</p></details></div></div></section><section class="resource-cta section"><div class="site-shell"><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("Free inspection")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Photos, report, estimated measurements and a written project path.")</h2><a class="button button-gold" href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc#claim-form">@Lang.T("Start my request →")</a></div></section>
